From 191ac24fb96cb56df5c52fe5c897844bcbae3115 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dario Gabriel Lipicar <dario@status.im>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 00:20:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] lightwalletd: hand the gRPC service to an embedder
 in-process

The lightwalletd server's documentation says not to run it on end users'
machines: a loopback port is reachable by any local process, and by web
pages loaded in a browser there. An application that embeds the node, and
already has a transport of its own between its processes, needs the
service rather than the port.

server::service() builds the CompactTxStreamer service that init() serves
over TCP. run_node() takes an optional sink that receives the same service,
type-erased and behind the same request tracing, whether or not
lightwalletd_listen_addr is set. StartCmd::start passes None, so zebrad
itself behaves as before.
---
 zebra-rpc/src/lightwalletd/server.rs | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 zebrad/src/commands/start.rs         | 42 +++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 77 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

